-- title:
--   From smooth-point stalks to smooth-point packages at q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $L:=\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $\kappa:=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ for the valuation subring $A$ below, $\bar{\mathcal M}:=\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$ is the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ over $L$ obtained by base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldFull}\ M'=\mathbb Q(\mathtt{divisorExpansions}\ M')\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\mathbb Q)$ along the coefficientwise embedding, and $F:=\mathtt{fieldBar}\ q\ M'=\mathtt{xHFunctionFieldBar}\ (q^2M')\ (\mathtt{levelH}\ q\ M')$ is the analogous base change of the function field of $X_{H}$ at level $q^2M'$ with $H=\mathtt{levelH}\ q\ M'$ the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** A prime $q$ with $q=3$; a nonzero $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$; a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$; a valuation subring $A$ of $L$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$ (the predicate `LiesOverPrime`); a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\ \kappa\ M'=\kappa(j,j_{M'})$ over $\kappa$ whose members are, by `hW`, exactly the elements of $\mathtt{ssPlaces}\ q\ M'\ \kappa$, that is the places $w$ that are rational (the structure map $\kappa\to w.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ is surjective), satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and have $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathtt{jGeomGen})\in\mathtt{ssJSet}\ q\ \kappa$; the inclusion `hle` of intermediate fields $\bar{\mathcal M}\le F$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from $\bar{\mathcal M}$ to $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\ \kappa\ M'$ (a valuation subring of integers with a surjective residue map onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants, together with the scaling and place-map clauses of `ConstantReduction`), subject to the compatibility `hR₀`: every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ lies in $\bar{\mathcal M}$ belongs to the integers of $R_0$, and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$; and a chosen $s\in W$.
--
--   **Small-field data.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q\subseteq L$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$, such that the valuation subring $A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to L$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian local, and has algebraically closed residue field; and `hκ`: every $a\in A$ agrees modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ with some element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary level data.** A prime $\ell$ with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\neq q$, $\ell\nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ whose image in $L$ is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; and $\varpi_t\in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **Layers.** A type $\iota$, a family $K:\iota\to$ intermediate fields of $k_0\subseteq L$ with each $K_n$ finite over $k_0$, and valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K_n$ with $x\in A_n\iff x\in A$ for all $x\in K_n$.
--
--   With the $k_0$-algebra structure on $F$ obtained by composing $k_0\to L$ with $L\to F$, the assertion is the following implication, for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0\subseteq F$ with $\mathrm{adjoin}_{k_0}(\mathrm{range}(L\to F))\sqcup F_0=\top$, every field $\mathrm{FSS}$ with a $\kappa$-algebra structure, and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from $F$ to $\mathrm{FSS}$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ with a surjective residue map to $\mathrm{FSS}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants, plus the scaling clause of `RegularProlongation`). Write $E_n:=\mathrm{adjoin}_{k_0}\big(\text{image of }K_n\text{ in }F\big)\sqcup F_0$.
--
--   **The Drinfeld clause (D), common to both sides.** For every $\mathtt{GaloisField}\ q\ 2$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every proof that $\mathtt{DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing}\ q\ \kappa$ is a domain, and every $\zeta\in\mathtt{Idx}\ q$ (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $L$), there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e$ from $\mathrm{FSS}$ onto $\mathtt{DrinfeldCurve.quotField}\ q\ \kappa\ C_s$, the fixed field inside the Drinfeld function field $\mathrm{Frac}(\mathtt{CoordRing}\ q\ \kappa)$ of the group generated by the actions of the elements of $C_s$, such that $\#C_s=2\cdot\mathtt{placeWidthChar}\ q\ M'\ s$ (the quotient of $\mathtt{jWidthChar}\ q$ at $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathtt{jGeomGen})$, which for $q=3$ is $6$ at $j=0$ and $1$ otherwise, by $\mathtt{placeRamificationJ}\ M'\ s$), and such that for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\subseteq\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, given that $\mathtt{levelAutBar}\ q\ M'\ \zeta\ \gamma^{-1}$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and that $(\mathtt{redQ}\ q\ \gamma,1)$ lies in $\mathtt{DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup}\ q$ (the kernel of $(g,u)\mapsto\det(g)\,u^{q+1}$), the automorphism $R.\mathrm{resAut}$ induced on $\mathrm{FSS}$ by $\mathtt{levelAutBar}\ q\ M'\ \zeta\ \gamma^{-1}$ is carried by $e$ to the action of $\langle(\mathtt{redQ}\ q\ \gamma,1)\rangle$ through $\mathtt{hFunctionFieldAction}\ q\ \kappa$, as an identity in the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   **The antecedent (stalks).** Clause (D) holds, and there exist a finite set $N$ of places of $\mathrm{FSS}$ over $\kappa$, subrings $S_{Q,n}\subseteq F$, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_{Q,n}:(A_n)[X]\to S_{Q,n}$ and $\chi_{Q,n}:S_{Q,n}\to\kappa$, and sets $D_{Q,n}$ of places of $F$ over $L$, such that:
--
--   (1) $\#N=q+1$;
--
--   (2) (affine chart) there is a subring $B\subseteq F$ with $B\subseteq R.\mathrm{integers}$, with $B\subseteq S_{Q,n}$ for all $Q\notin N$ and all $n$, and such that every $z\in\mathrm{FSS}$ lying in the valuation subring of every $Q\notin N$ is the $R$-residue of some $f\in B$;
--
--   (3) for every $Q\notin N$: first, for every $n$,
--   (S1) the map $A_n\to\kappa$, $a\mapsto$ residue of $a$ in $A$, is surjective;
--   (S2) the image of $A_n$ in $F$ lies in $S_{Q,n}$;
--   (S3) $\varphi_{Q,n}$ is formally smooth and formally unramified;
--   (S4) $\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$ in $F$, for $a\in A_n$;
--   (S5) $\chi_{Q,n}(\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$;
--   (S6) $\chi_{Q,n}(\varphi_{Q,n}(X))=0$;
--   (S7) for every $c\in A_n$ with zero residue there is a unique ring homomorphism $\chi:S_{Q,n}\to A_n$ with $\chi(\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,a))=a$ for all $a\in A_n$, with residue of $\chi(f)$ equal to $\chi_{Q,n}(f)$ for all $f$, and with $\chi(\varphi_{Q,n}(X))=c$;
--   (S8) every $f\in S_{Q,n}$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the residue there equals the image of $\chi_{Q,n}(f)$ under $\kappa\to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$;
--   (S9) $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R$-residue has $Q$-order $1$;
--   (S10) $P\in D_{Q,n}$ if and only if $P$ is rational, every $f\in S_{Q,n}$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$, and for every $f\in S_{Q,n}$ one has $A.\mathrm{valuation}(P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f))<1$ exactly when $\chi_{Q,n}(f)=0$;
--   (S11) $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)\neq\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,c)$ for every $c\in A_n$;
--   (S12) $S_{Q,n}$ is local with maximal ideal the kernel of $\chi_{Q,n}$, Noetherian, and a unique factorisation monoid;
--   (S13) $S_{Q,n}\subseteq E_n$;
--   (S14) every $f\in E_n$ satisfies $f\,h=g$ for some $g,h\in S_{Q,n}$ with $h\neq0$;
--   (S15) for every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to L$ linearly independent over $K_n$ and every $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to F$ with all $a_i\in E_n$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ forces $a_i=0$ for all $i$;
--   (S16) for every ring homomorphism $\chi:S_{Q,n}\to A_n$ splitting $\varphi_{Q,n}\circ C$ and inducing $\chi_{Q,n}$ on residues, $\ker\chi$ is generated by $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)-\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,\chi(\varphi_{Q,n}(X)))$;
--   (S17) there is a uniformiser $\varpi$ of $A_n$, nonzero and generating the maximal ideal, such that $\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,\varpi)$ is prime in $S_{Q,n}$, such that an $f\in E_n$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when $f\,h=g$ for some $g,h\in S_{Q,n}$ with $\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,\varpi)\nmid h$, and such that for every prime $p$ of $S_{Q,n}$ not associated to $\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,\varpi)$ and every $x\in S_{Q,n}$ there is a monic $r\in (A_n)[X]$ with $p$ dividing the value at $x$ of $r$ pushed forward along $\varphi_{Q,n}\circ C$;
--   (S18) there is a finite $G\subseteq S_{Q,n}$ such that every $f\in S_{Q,n}$ satisfies $f\,h=g$ with $g,h$ in the subring generated by $G$ together with the image of $A_n$, and $h$ a unit of $S_{Q,n}$;
--   and second, the layers are compatible: there is a monotonicity witness $S_{Q,n}\subseteq S_{Q,n'}$ whenever $K_n\le K_{n'}$, for such $n,n'$ one has $S_{Q,n'}\subseteq$ the subring generated by $S_{Q,n}$ and the image of $A_{n'}$, the elements $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)$ agree in $F$ for all $n$, and $\chi_{Q,n'}$ restricts to $\chi_{Q,n}$ on $S_{Q,n}$;
--
--   (4) for $Q,Q'\notin N$, if some place $P$ lies in $D_{Q,n}\cap D_{Q',n}$ for some $n$, then $Q=Q'$;
--
--   (5) for $Q\notin N$, every $n$ and every $P\in D_{Q,n}$, the order $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the element of $F$ obtained from the $q$-expansion $\mathtt{jq}$ of $j$ (its coefficientwise image in $\bar{\mathcal M}$, included into $F$ via `hle`) is $\ge 0$;
--
--   (6) for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $L$-automorphisms of $F$ generated by the automorphisms $\mathtt{levelAutBar}\ q\ M'\ \zeta\ \gamma$ with $\zeta\in\mathtt{Idx}\ q$ and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, and every proof that $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$: for every place $Q$ one has $R.\mathrm{resAut}(\tau)\cdot Q\in N$ if and only if $Q\in N$, and if $Q\notin N$ then for every $n$ the translate $\mathtt{smulDisc}\ \tau\ (D_{Q,n})=\{P: \tau^{-1}\cdot P\in D_{Q,n}\}$ equals $D_{R.\mathrm{resAut}(\tau)\cdot Q,\,n}$.
--
--   **The consequent (packages).** Clause (D) holds verbatim as above, and there exist data $N,S_{Q,n},\varphi_{Q,n},\chi_{Q,n},D_{Q,n}$ of the same types (quantified anew) satisfying clauses (1) and (2) verbatim, and, for every $Q\notin N$ and every $n$, clauses (S1)–(S10) verbatim, together with:
--
--   (P11) for every ring homomorphism $\chi:S_{Q,n}\to A_n$ splitting $\varphi_{Q,n}\circ C$ and inducing $\chi_{Q,n}$ on residues, there is a unique place $P\in D_{Q,n}$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)=\chi(f)$ in $L$ for all $f\in S_{Q,n}$;
--
--   (P12) for every $P\in D_{Q,n}$ and every $f\in E_n$: $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ if and only if $f\,h=g$ for some $g,h\in S_{Q,n}$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(h)\neq0$;
--
--   (P13) every nonzero $f\in E_n$ with $P.\mathrm{ord}(f)=0$ for all $P\in D_{Q,n}$ satisfies $c\,f=u$ for some nonzero $c\in K_n$ (via its image in $F$) and some unit $u$ of $S_{Q,n}$;
--
--   (P14) every $f\in E_n$ that lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and in the valuation subring of every $P\in D_{Q,n}$ lies in $S_{Q,n}$;
--
--   (P15) clause (S18) verbatim;
--
--   furthermore, for every $Q\notin N$, the layer-compatibility clause stated in (3) verbatim, and clauses (4), (5) and (6) verbatim.
--
--   Thus the algebraic description of the stalks — local ring with residue map $\chi_{Q,n}$, Noetherian, factorial, the kernel and uniformiser clauses, the linear-disjointness and fraction clauses, and the non-degeneracy $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)\neq\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,c)$ — is traded for the geometric description of the residue discs $D_{Q,n}$: existence and uniqueness of the point with prescribed section values, the fractional description of each $P$-integrality, the unit principle on the disc, and the recovery of $S_{Q,n}$ as the sections integral at $R$ and regular on the whole disc.
--
--   This is the functorial step, for $q=3$ at a rigid auxiliary level, that upgrades a stalkwise description of the smooth points of the supersingular component at level $q^2M'$ (local rings $S_{Q,n}$ with residue characters $\chi_{Q,n}$) to a package description in terms of the residue discs $D_{Q,n}$, uniformly in the layers $K_n$ and for every regular prolongation $R$ and every complementary field $F_0$. The engine is [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.disc_sections_locality_of_smoothPoint`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.disc_sections_locality_of_smoothPoint), applied with the curve and principality inputs coming from [`ModularCurve.isCurveOver_and_essFiniteType_laurentBaseChange_xHFunctionField`](thm.html#ModularCurve.isCurveOver_and_essFiniteType_laurentBaseChange_xHFunctionField), [`ModularCurve.JOneES.exists_transcendental_finiteDimensional_laurentBaseChange`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JOneES.exists_transcendental_finiteDimensional_laurentBaseChange) and [`ValuationSubring.isPrincipalIdealRing_of_finiteDimensional_adjoin`](thm.html#ValuationSubring.isPrincipalIdealRing_of_finiteDimensional_adjoin); the result feeds the construction of the $q=3$ supersingular column used downstream.
